-- Ruled by Meng 2026-11-21, extending L2 (smucclaw/l4-ide#1075): l4 coverage counts. The
-- decision's condition applies two functions at each input, so under
-- --max-steps 1 every input it tries stops at the limit. That the decision
-- is then not covered, with the stop as the reason, and that a stopped input
-- is never read as one at which the condition raises, are decided by Claude 2026-11-21, pending Meng's review (L2 extension, choice 2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`double` n MEANS n PLUS n

@export Which band a number falls into.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`band` n MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF `double` (`double` n) GREATER THAN 100 THEN 2
    OTHERWISE                                       1
